  tutorialClip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 333ece54758137a42a55ee10d76b738d, type: 3}
  subtitleList:
  - "Howdy, cadet. Name\u2019s John\u2014your guide through this flight."
  - See those cheerful little planes flying in formation around us?
  - "Those are our wingmen, and they\u2019re tuned in to your BCI thingy\u2014that
    brain-reading gizmo you\u2019ve got hooked up."
  - "Each one is keeping watch over not just one\u2014but two of your brain sensors."
  - "That\u2019s why they\u2019ve got numbers on their tail fins\u2014like \u201C1.2\u201D
    or \u201C3.4\u201D\u2014each pair shows which electrodes they\u2019re watching"
  - "If one starts bobbing through turbulence, it means one of its signal\u2019s
    getting jittery."
  - "And if it vanishes from the sky, that signal\u2019s gone dark."
  - "Right now, they\u2019re all flying smooth and steady\u2014that means everything's
    in working order, and you're in full control."
  - "Keep it that way, and we\u2019ll have a fine flight ahead."
